IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `acl-consumer`

-- Competition and Consumer Act 2010 (Cth), Sch 2 ss 3, 18, 23-27, 50, 54-59, 64, 64A, 69, 73, 75, 82, 85, 86, 259-263; ss 131, 131A; Part IVA; Regulations regs 77A, 81, 95 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case. The Competition and Consumer Regulations 2010 are deposited and used.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_competition-and-consumer-act-2010_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-*): Chloe's new laptop fails in month three and the
-- retailer repairs it on 20 May 2032 (c070). Jarrah, Daniel's company, registered March 2031 with three employees from June,
-- reviews its standard software terms with a liability cap at the subscription fee on 10 July 2031 (d045). A competitor
-- trades as JARRA, a letter, a rebrand, 11 February 2039 (d056). Jarrah acquires Formly Pty Ltd on 15 June 2043, 'not
-- notifiable at this size' (d065). Jake owes $41,000 and collectors call on 6 February 2037 (k064); he took two credit
-- cards in March 2031 (k048). The lives give no laptop price or purchase date, no customer or contract price, no turnover,
-- no figure for Formly and no account of what the collectors did: those figures are ASSUMED, and each judgment the Act
-- leaves to a court (acceptable quality, major failure, unfair, misleading, undue harassment) is set by hand.

